- Updated difficulty levels: Normal, Difficult and five Nightmare levels. Passing them you get more ingame experience; 

About what was added and what to expect from the recent update read below: 

New items: Knight set
Knight’s amulet: Energy +1. If health is >80%, energy +2;
Knight’s sabaton: Health +15. If the health is >80%, it gives 3 cards at the beginning of the turn;
Knight's armor: Health +30. If your health is >80%, Armor +10;
Knight's helmet: Health +15. If health is >80%, Strength +3 and Agility +3;
Knight Shield: If health >80%, Agility +3;
Knight Sword: If health >80%, Power +3;

   -Normal (current)
   -Difficult: Enemy health is increased, enemies do more damage;
   -Nightmares: The effects of each new nightmare level are added to the previous ones;
   -Nightmare 1: Enemies get random buff;
   -Nightmare 2: Random events are less likely to have chests;
   -Nightmare 3: Traders are less likely to be caught in random events;
   -Nightmare 4: Random events are more likely to have battles;
   -Nightmare 5: Elite battles are encountered in questions marks;

New skills: 
Gold seeker:
1 time per move gives a card "At Energy 0, restore all energy and give as many cards" price of 30 gold;
Gold in awards +50;
Gives a card Hit the wallet (price 0, spends 20% of gold, deals 20% damage to gold);
Gives a Gold Shield card (price 0, spends 20% of gold, gives a block at 20% of gold);
For every 100 gold in the deck, the Greed card... (unplayable);
Knight:
If Health >80%, Power +1, Agility +1, Energy +1, +1 card;
The cards from the reset are placed in the deck in the same order as they were in the reset;
If there are no two cards of the same type in the hand at the beginning of the turn, the player receives 2 energy and 10 health;
Veteran:
Energy +3. At the beginning of a turn it restores 1 Energy (instead of all);
The energy does not reset at the end of the stroke;
Using 3 different types of cards reduces the cost of other cards in the hand by 1;
Using 2 cards of the same type increases the cost of cards in hand by 1;


